# Full vibrational Raman of LiH -- the smallest full-tensor Raman deck.
# One rung (protocol 1e-4, k 6): alpha(0) xyz, the complete static
# polarizability gradient over all 3N = 6 nuclear coordinates
# (raman.nuc_atom -1), the Hessian built from the same six nuclear response
# states, the one vibrational mode, and its Raman activity and depolarization
# ratio. Legs: 3 dipole + 6 nuclear-displacement; 18 quadratic sources.
#
# Response dconv 1e-4: the FD gate is relative (||dx|| <= atol + 5 dconv ||x||),
# so the ~1e3-norm nuclear-displacement legs converge at the same dconv as the
# dipole legs (under the earlier absolute gate they needed dconv 1e-3).
# The numbers are a regression baseline at k 6, not converged Raman values.
# The removed molresponse_v2 engine gave, at protocol [1e-4, 1e-5] and l 80:
# one mode at 1427.94 cm^-1, activity 350.59 A^4/amu, depolarization 0.0323.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=response response_lih_raman_full.in)

dft
    xc        hf
    dconv     1e-4
    k         6
    protocol  [1e-4]
    l         50.0
    localize  new
    maxiter   30
end

response
    dipole                true
    dipole.directions     xyz
    dipole.frequencies    [0.0]
    requested_properties  [polarizability, raman]
    raman.nuc_atom        -1
    kain                  true
    dconv                 1e-4
    maxiter               60
    print_level           1
end

molecule
    eprec      1e-6
    no_orient  true
    units      angstrom
    Li  0.0  0.0  -0.803105264950
    H   0.0  0.0   0.803105264950
end
